Pre-release audit finding (0.600 -> 0.601). cpanfile already lists several core modules explicitly (Errno, POSIX, Sys::Hostname, Time::HiRes, IO::Select, IO::Handle, Encode, Scalar::Util) even though they ship with Perl -- that is this project's own convention for completeness. Six more core modules are used directly in lib/ but are not in cpanfile, breaking that consistency:

  - Carp (lib/App/karr/Task.pm)
  - Digest::MD5 (lib/App/karr/Foundation.pm, lib/App/karr/Foundation/ChainStore.pm)
  - Exporter (lib/App/karr/AgentName.pm, Error.pm, Dispatch.pm, Encoding.pm)
  - Fcntl (lib/App/karr/Foundation/Agents.pm, Foundation/State.pm)
  - IPC::Open3 (lib/App/karr/Git.pm)
  - Symbol (lib/App/karr/Git.pm)

Not an installability blocker (all ship with every Perl, and dzil build already completes cleanly via Prereqs::FromCPANfile), but add requires lines for these six, alphabetically among the existing core-module entries, for consistency with the stated house rule that every actually-used runtime dep is declared.

